            <ArticleTitle>An Innovative and Successful Simulation Day.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>96-97</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NEP.0000000000000107</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article discusses the development of a creative and innovative plan to incorporate independent activities, including skill reviews and scenarios, into a single eight-hour day, using small student groups to enhance the learning process for pediatric nursing students. The simulation day consists of skills activities and pediatric simulation scenarios using the human patient simulator. Using small student groups in simulation captures the students' attention and enhances motivation to learn. The simulation day is a work in progress; appropriate changes are continually being made to improve the simulation experience for students.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
